      <h2 class="text-primary-text font-bold mb-6">
        The Best Locations for a Romantic Photoshoot for Couples in London
      </h2>

      <p class="text-secondary-text mb-12">
        London is full of amazing outdoor locations that are perfect for a
        romantic photoshoot. Whether you prefer grand parks, riverside views, or
        hidden gardens, the city has something for every couple. Here are a few
        of my favourite spots:
      </p>

      <ol class="text-secondary-text mb-6 ml-6 list-decimal space-y-4">
        <li>
          <strong>Richmond Park</strong> - Richmond Park offers a nice setting with
          wide open spaces, ancient trees, and beautiful deer roaming freely. It's
          the ideal spot for couples who love nature and want a peaceful, secluded
          feel for their photoshoot.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Holland Park</strong> - For a touch of elegance, Holland Park's
          beautiful gardens, especially the Kyoto Garden, make for a romantic backdrop.
          The combination of serene ponds, bright flowers, and quiet walkways creates
          a timeless, romantic atmosphere.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Canbury Gardens</strong> - If you're after a peaceful spot, Canbury
          Gardens is perfect. Nestled by the River Thames in Kingston, it offers serene
          riverside views, tree-lined paths, and soft greenery, making it an ideal
          backdrop for capturing intimate moments. It's the perfect place to reflect
          your love story in a calm and natural setting.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bushy Park</strong> - Just like Richmond Park, Bushy Park has wide-open
          spaces, beautiful pathways, and lots of natural beauty. It's also less crowded,
          making it perfect for a more private and intimate photoshoot.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hyde Park</strong> - One of London's most famous parks, Hyde Park,
          offers a mix of natural beauty and iconic spots like the Serpentine Lake.
          Whether it's a quiet moment by the water or a stroll through the trees,
          Hyde Park has endless possibilities for romantic photos.
        </li>
      </ol>

