      <h2 class="text-primary-text font-bold mb-6">
        When Is the Best Time for a Romantic Photoshoot?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-secondary-text mb-6">
        While golden hour (just before sunset) is known for its soft, flattering
        light, the best time for your romantic photoshoot is whenever you and
        your partner feel most comfortable. If you're early risers, a morning
        shoot with the soft, dewy light can be just as magical as an evening
        one. The key is working around your schedule and choosing a time that
        suits your vibe.
      </p>

      <p class="text-secondary-text mb-12">
        That said, we'll avoid the harsh midday light, which can create strong
        shadows and make you squint. Whether it's a crisp autumn morning or a
        warm summer evening, we'll find the perfect time to capture those
        beautiful, glowing images that you'll cherish.
      </p>

